[22.077, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\nThe **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) is the tool for this \u2014 it executes SQL queries and dry-runs against BigQuery directly. It requires GCP auth. Let me check your current\r\n"]
[22.877, "o", "The tool is the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** \u2014 it runs live SQL queries, inspects schemas, and provides dry-run cost estimates on BigQuery.\r\n\r\nHowever, your environment has **no GCP authentication** (no gcloud CLI, no ADC, no service account), so it isn't ready to use. You'd need to onboard first (install gcloud + `gcloud auth application-default login`), or use the free tier (~1TB/month of query processing).\r\n\r\nTwo immediate no-auth alternatives:\r\n- **BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines skill** \u2014 offline guidance for writing optimized queries on large datasets.\r\n- **Google Developer Knowledge MCP** \u2014 docs/API lookup for BigQuery.\r\n\r\nWant me to record that you'd like to onboard for BigQuery so I can give you the exact setup commands?\r\n"]
[23.677, "o", "\u001b[?2004hdeveloper@workstation:~/ard-project$ "]
