[36.208, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"query public BigQuery dataset SQL\"}\r\n"]
[37.008, "o", "Let me check your current auth status to see which tool is\r\n"]
[37.105, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n"]
[37.905, "o", "The **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) is the tool for this. It can execute SQL queries, inspect schemas, explore public datasets, and estimate costs.\r\n\r\nHowever, it requires GCP auth (Tier 3), and your environment has **no gcloud/credentials** yet. A fallback that works immediately with no auth is the **BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines Skill**.\r\n\r\nWant me to record your consent to onboard the BigQuery MCP server? You'd then run `gcloud auth application-default login` in your terminal to connect.\r\n"]
[38.705, "o", "\u001b[?2004hdeveloper@workstation:~/ard-project$ "]
