[42.499, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n"]
[43.299, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_record_decision {\"service_identifier\":\"urn:ai:google.com:mcp:google-cloud-discovery\",\"decision\":\"onboarded\"}\r\n"]
[44.099, "o", "Your onboarding decision is recorded. Here's how to log in \u2014 I'll guide you through it:\r\n\r\n**1. Install the Google Cloud CLI** (needed first, since `gcloud` isn't detected on this machine):\r\n\r\n- macOS: `brew install --cask google-cloud-sdk`\r\n- Linux: follow the instructions at https://cloud.google.com/sdk/docs/install\r\n- Windows: download the installer from https://cloud.google.com/sdk/docs/install\r\n\r\n**2. Once installed, run these in your terminal:**\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ngcloud auth login                # browser-based login\r\ngcloud auth application-default login   # ADC for tools/APIs (Tier 3)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**3. Set your project (optional but recommended):**\r\n```bash\r\ngcloud config set project YOUR_PROJECT_ID\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter you've run those, let me know and I'll re-check your auth status. Alternatively, if you have a service account JSON key, point me to it and I'll activate it.\r\n"]
[44.899, "o", "\u001b[?2004hdeveloper@workstation:~/ard-project$ "]
