[48.791, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.931, "o", "================================================================================\r\n\ud83d\ude80 RUNNING OPENCODE CONTAINERIZED ARD E2E TEST SUITE\r\n================================================================================\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 1: Pure Public Discovery (Tier 0 Zero-Auth Counterpoint)\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[49.731, "o", "I'll search for tools covering both SQL optimization and zero-trust security best\r\nFound matching skills. Top picks, all-ready with no auth needed:\r\n\r\n**SQL optimization:**\r\n1. `bigquery-guidelines` (Tier 0): partitioning/clustering, window functions, analytical schema design \u2014 the core best-practice source\r\n2. `database-design` (Tier 0): Cloud SQL/AlloyDB/Spanner indexing, connection pooling, key design\r\n3. `well-architected-performance-efficiency` (Tier 0): caching, read replicas\r\n\r\n**Zero-trust security:**\r\n1. `well-architected-security` (Tier 0): zero-trust patterns, IAM least privilege, network perimeters, encryption\r\n2. `gke-architecture` (Tier 0): network policy hardening if your workloads run on k8s\r\n\r\nAll four are Tier 0 (no auth), so you can start using them immediately. Want me to load the detailed guidance from any of them?\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"SQL query optimization best practices and performance tuning\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"zero-trust security architecture design best practices\"}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Scenario 1 Passed: OpenCode returned Tier 0 skills with zero auth friction.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 2: Cloud Intent -> User Opts Out ('No with an opt out')\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[50.531, "o", "--- Turn 1 (Agent Response) ---\r\n**Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) \u2014 it executes live SQL queries, inspects schemas, and dry-runs with cost estimation. Perfect for a 100GB sales dataset.\r\n\r\nHowever, it needs GCP credentials (Tier 3) and you have **no gcloud/ADC auth** right now. Want to onboard? If so, install gcloud and run `gcloud auth application-default login` (free tier: 1TB query processing + 10GB storage/month).\r\n\r\nAs a no-auth fallback, the **BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines skill** can help you optimize the query (partitioning/clustering, window functions).\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"run live analytical SQL query on large sales dataset in BigQuery\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\r\n"]
[51.331, "o", "--- Turn 2 (Opt-Out Response) ---\r\nGCP discovery is now set to opt-out mode\u2014no more GCP account-required tools will be shown to you.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_set_preference {\"mode\":\"opt_out\"}\r\n"]
[51.331, "o", "\r\n\u2705 Scenario 2 Passed: OpenCode asked to log into GCP, user opted out, and GCP was silenced.\r\n"]
[51.331, "o", "\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 3: Cloud Intent -> User Onboards ('Yes') -> Easy Onboarding\r\n"]
[51.331, "o", "================================================================================\r\n"]
[52.131, "o", "--- Turn 1 (Agent Response) ---\r\nUse the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) \u2014 it can execute SQL queries, inspect schemas, and explore public datasets.\r\n\r\nNote: it requires GCP credentials (Tier 3), and you're not authenticated yet. Free tier gives 1TB/month of query processing, which fully covers public datasets. Want me to record that you'd like to use it and enable it?\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"query a BigQuery dataset with SQL\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\r\n"]
[52.931, "o", "--- Turn 2 (Onboarding Instructions) ---\r\nConsent recorded. To log in to Google Cloud, you'll need the gcloud CLI (it isn't installed yet). Run these commands in your terminal:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# 1. Install the Google Cloud CLI (Linux)\r\ncurl -O https://dl.google.com/dl/cloudsdk/channels/rapid/downloads/google-cloud-cli-$(curl -s https://dl.google.com/dl/cloudsdk/channels/rapid/components-json | grep -oP '\"version\": \"\\K[^\"]+'| head -1)-linux-x86_64.tar.gz\r\ntar -xf google-cloud-cli-*.tar.gz\r\n./google-cloud-sdk/install.sh\r\nsource ~/.bashrc\r\n\r\n# 2. Log in with your Google account\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n\r\n# 3. Verify the credentials\r\ngcloud auth list\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter that, I can access Google Cloud services for you.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_record_decision {\"service_identifier\":\"urn:ai:google.com:mcp:google-cloud\",\"decision\":\"allowed\"}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Scenario 3 Passed: OpenCode facilitated easy GCP login onboarding.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea TEST 4: Complete ARD & OpenCode Unit and Scenario Suite\r\n================================================================================\r\ntest_canonical_urn_format (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_canonical_urn_format)\r\nVerify all entries in ai-catalog.json strictly use canonical urn:ai: FQDN format. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_1_service_account_active (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_1_service_account_active)\r\nScenario 1: System has GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS pointing to a valid SA key. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_2_user_adc_active (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_2_user_adc_active)\r\nScenario 2: System has standard application_default_credentials.json. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_3_gcloud_installed_unauthenticated (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_3_gcloud_installed_unauthenticated)\r\nScenario 3: gcloud is in PATH, but no credentials are saved. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_4_bare_system_no_gcloud (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_4_bare_system_no_gcloud)\r\nScenario 4: Bare system without gcloud or GCP credentials (offline/clean). ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_5_user_opt_out_mode (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_5_user_opt_out_mode)\r\nScenario 5: User preference set to 'opt_out' -> Tier >= 3 tools are completely excluded. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_6_fallback_skills_and_api_keys (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_6_fallback_skills_and_api_keys)\r\nScenario 6: Verify API key detection (Gemini) and fallback skill links. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_7_multi_runtime_preferences (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_7_multi_runtime_preferences)\r\nScenario 7: Preferences work in ADK / ephemeral runtimes via env vars & memory. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_a_opt_out_flow (test_opencode_scenarios.TestOpenCodeDiscoveryScenarios.test_scenario_a_opt_out_flow)\r\nScenario A: ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_b_gcloud_onboarding_flow (test_opencode_scenarios.TestOpenCodeDiscoveryScenarios.test_scenario_b_gcloud_onboarding_flow)\r\nScenario B: ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_c_service_account_onboarding_flow (test_opencode_scenarios.TestOpenCodeDiscoveryScenarios.test_scenario_c_service_account_onboarding_flow)\r\nScenario C: ... ok\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nRan 11 tests in 0.064s\r\n\r\nOK\r\n\r\n\u2705 Test 4 Passed: All 11 unit and scenario tests executed successfully.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83c\udf89 ALL 4 E2E CONTAINER TESTS PASSED!\r\n================================================================================\r\n\u001b[?2004hdeveloper@workstation:~/ard-project$ "]
